## HOLDS
1. **Every records-file write (CLARIFICATIONS.md, HISTORY.md, your STATUS, a kit copy): build AND ENCODE the whole new content first, write it to a temp file beside the target, then `os.replace` it; never open the live file for writing before the content exists, and never encode the whole file as ASCII when the file already holds non-ASCII bytes (encode the ADDED bytes and check them). Then `cmp` the prefix against a before-copy.** (2026-11-18: an earlier pass's append helper left this file at 0 bytes for about a minute. The same rule covers HISTORY.md in your worktree.)
2. No Jira write outside the closed list; no GitHub write at all except Step 7's one branch; no statement that anything is built, put on a host, fixed or proven that a record or a read does not show; **nothing is put in the product owner's mouth: no text quotes or paraphrases an answer of his; the field order, the UTC re-pin, the buckets and the 22:00 edge are defaults of the change**; no alert read as a landing condition on a pull request head; **no comment says the page was seen in a browser, claims Release Ready, says the demo shows a figure it was not shown to show, or says the Build of pull request 257 passed before it concluded**; no person's name, B-number, seat id or card id in any Jira or repo text; the noreply id is never written into Jira, `CLARIFICATIONS.md` or `HISTORY.md` and never printed. **OUT OF SCOPE, named:** any code change; anything put on a host; any message to a human; chasing an alert or re-running any job; a config write; a ticket for any finding but the two of THE NEW TICKETS (the two parser shapes, the other readers, the cosmetic tags are not ticketed by this pass); any comment on RD-695, RD-688, RD-975, RD-980, RD-1037, RD-1041 or on a found duplicate; an edit of any earlier entry, history text or ticket description; a label edit on an existing key; **a deploy decision, or a statement that anything should or should not be put on a host**; HPSM-POC, OXPd, Composer. A failed post, move or comment: stop that item, find the root cause, re-verify; never retry blindly. **Git identity is never overridden:** the repo's own configured identity only; never `git -c user.name/user.email`, never `GIT_AUTHOR_*` / `GIT_COMMITTER_*`; the READY section prints equality and sha256 prefixes of author and committer of the new commit, each equal to the repo's configured email. **PRIOR-WORK CHECK (standing line):** a READY without `## PRIOR WORK` is returned. No message to any human. Jira writes only where this scope says. Never delete. Shell: no `cd`; absolute single-quoted paths; `python3 -I -B`; `/usr/bin/grep -i` with a positive control for every count; never a run of equals signs as a separator and never an unquoted word that starts with an equals sign (zsh expands it); never call a command held in an unquoted variable (zsh does not split it: write it out or wrap it in `bash -c`); never name a shell variable `path`; run multi-word loops under `bash`.
3. **A kit rule is never changed on the seat's own reading:** a check that does not run as this kit says, a literal that does not match, a count that differs from the kit's, a STOP rule that reads too strictly: it is a `STOPPED: NEEDS TUESDAY` question, never a rewrite by the seat. **Checks of this kit that have NEVER run on a real output** (the drafter ran only its scan, its pointer program, its repeated-text check, its simulated append, its dup-check and its searches): your ADF builder, the posting path, the append helper, the check over added lines on a real fill-in, the Step 7 helper and its history scan, the FOR TUESDAY lister, the EVIDENCE poll, the dup-check guard on a real run: **a failure you can trace to this kit's own wording is a `STOPPED: NEEDS TUESDAY` question.**
4. **What a FAIL in your own helper allows.** (a) A selftest FAIL that traces to YOUR helper (not to this kit): fix the helper, then re-run the WHOLE group once more, never only the helpers you touched, print both group counts, and name every edit in Deviations; nothing is posted before a group reads 0 FAIL. (b) No helper is edited after its group has read 0 FAIL and a real read or write has used it; a real-run defect found later is a `STOPPED: NEEDS TUESDAY` question unless it is a fault in the helper that stops a write BEFORE any POST (then one edit, the whole group re-run, named). (c) The dup-check guard reads THE NEW TICKETS' REVIEWED list from the start. (d) Every fill-in clause is whole and carries a value only once; the template holds no run id; the HELD forms are checked too. (e) Every count of this kit is printed in THE WORK's list from the drafter's program; a count your own helper computes differently is printed beside the kit's and named in Deviations, never silently "corrected".

